Bundled third-party components
------------------------------
* **No video decoder is bundled any more** (27.1.3): the built-in JCodec-based converter and the
  MJPEG / ZIP frame-sequence backend were removed. Video playback is delegated to the optional
  WaterMedia mod at runtime (see below).
* Audio decoders, used **only** by the music widget (see "Music module" below).
  They are embedded unmodified as separate jars in META-INF/jarjar/ and can be
  replaced individually, which is what the LGPL permits for a work that uses the library:
  - mp3spi 1.9.5.4, jlayer 1.0.1.4, tritonus-share 0.3.7.4 (MP3)
    — JavaZOOM, GNU LGPL 2.1. https://www.javazoom.net/
  - jflac-codec 1.5.3 (FLAC) — Josh Coalson / jFLAC project, BSD-style license.
  - javasound-aac 0.9.6, bundled with JAAD (AAC / M4A decoding, includes an MP4 container parser)
    — GNU LGPL 2.1. https://sourceforge.net/projects/jaadec/
  None of these libraries are modified, and none of their source is copied into
  this project's own source tree.
* Optional runtime interop with WaterMedia (https://modrinth.com/mod/watermedia):
  no source code, classes or binaries from that project are used, compiled against or
  bundled. When it happens to be installed, this mod calls its publicly documented API
  by reflection (name lookup at runtime) so its decoders can play common video formats.
  WaterMedia is licensed under PolyForm Strict 1.0.0, which is not compatible with this
  project's Apache-2.0; keeping the dependency optional and reflective is deliberate.
* Fonts shipped in assets/projector/font/ (minecraft.ttf, caviar_dreams.ttf)
  are the property of their respective authors and are not covered by
  the Apache License of this project. Verify their terms before redistributing.
* Minecraft, NeoForge and their logos are trademarks of their respective owners.
  This mod is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by Mojang or Microsoft.

Music module
-------------
The music widget's playback engine (audio stream decoding, HTTP range streaming,
ID3 skipping, NetEase Cloud Music API calls and LRC lyric parsing) is derived from
**Net Music Mod / 网络音乐机** by TartaricAcid and contributors
(https://github.com/TartaricAcid/NetMusic), which is published under the MIT License.
Files derived from it live in
src/main/java/top/hmjmfabc/projector/client/music/ and in the music branch of
client/gui/MusicPickerScreen.java.

Supported audio formats are MP3 / FLAC / WAV / **AAC and M4A** (27.1.3).
AAC/M4A had been dropped earlier because its decoder (javasound-aac, which contains JAAD)
declared the same JPMS packages as the JAAD classes bundled inside JCodec, and two jar-in-jar
libraries exporting the same package make ModLauncher fail at startup
(java.lang.module.ResolutionException). JCodec is no longer bundled, so the conflict is gone
and AAC/M4A is back. (Re-check for duplicate packages whenever a jar-in-jar is added.)

Only the music module references that project: every other part of this mod
(planes, widgets, rendering, media transfer, games, sequences, fonts) was written
independently and shares no code with it.

Online video module
-------------------
The online-video link resolver (Bilibili BV/av/短链/番剧/直播 与 yhdm 的接口调用与解析流程,
src/main/java/top/hmjmfabc/projector/common/OnlineVideoLink.java and
client/media/net/OnlineVideoResolver.java) was written after reading
**Bilibili Media KOTS / Bilibili-Media-Mod-2-neoforge** by Polaris_Light
(https://gitee.dev.polaris_light/bilibiliMediaNeo, https://modrinth.com/mod/bilibilimedia),
which is published under the MIT License.

No source file, class or binary from that project is copied, compiled against or bundled:
the referenced project is a Mixin plugin for WaterMedia, whereas this mod performs the same
public HTTP API calls with its own code, without Mixins and without linking WaterMedia.
Only the public Bilibili endpoints/parameters and the resulting resolution flow were used
as a reference.

MCEF (Minecraft Chromium Embedded Framework)
--------------------------------------------
Optional runtime dependency for the "web widget" (27.2). Copyright its authors (ds58 / CinemaMod),
licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License v2.1 (LGPL-2.1).

MCEF is NOT bundled, NOT compiled against and NOT linked: this mod contains no import of
com.cinemamod.mcef.* or org.cef.*, declares MCEF only as an optional loader dependency, and
reaches its public API exclusively through runtime reflection (Class.forName + getMethod).
No source file or code fragment of MCEF was copied into this project. Per MCEF's own README,
a project that neither modifies nor includes MCEF source code may use a different license.

On Android the official MCEF build is unsupported ("This mod will not work on Android");
players there additionally need the separate "MCEF: Android Bridge" compatibility mod, which
is likewise neither bundled nor linked by this project.

